{# §5 What's driving — three layers, all real.
   Reference: Sarreid PASS3 §5 (lines 95-130).

   Layer 1 = same-dealer base (Q-ECON-NRR / dealer cohort)
   Layer 2 = growth family (Q-PROD-FAMILY top-1 grower)
   Layer 3 = field team breakout (RS-01 top-3 by YoY %)

   FAMILY_COVERAGE_MIN_PCT (below = do not call it a topline "driver"): a family/collection
   grouping can be a real, broad-based growth pocket while covering a small slice of total
   invoiced revenue (cci: BUNNY WILLIAMS family = 2.4% of inv_ltm_net, audit_cci_mode1_2026-07-09.md
   §3.1). Below this threshold, Layer 2's title and framing downgrade from "the X family" /
   "driving the topline" to "a growth pocket" and disclose the coverage share, so the reader
   isn't told a rounding error is one of three things running the business. #}
